===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃ekʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|eye}}, {{m|enm|eie}}, {{m|enm|yë}}, {{m|enm|eighe}}, {{m|enm|eyghe}}, {{m|enm|yȝe}}, {{m|enm|eyȝe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ēaġe|t=eye}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*augā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*augô|t=eye}} (compare {{cog|sco|ee}}, {{cog|fy|each}}, {{cog|nl|oog}}, {{cog|de|Auge}}, {{cog|da|øje}}, {{cog|nb|øye}}, {{cog|nn|auga}}, {{cog|sv|öga}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₃okʷ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ekʷ-|t=eye; to see}}.

Other {{cog|ine}} cognates include {{cog|la|oculus}} (whence {{cog|en|oculus}}), {{cog|lt|akìs}}, {{cog|cu|око}}, {{cog|sq|sy}}, {{cog|grc|ὄψ||(''poetic'') eye; face|id=eye}} and {{m|grc|ὄσσε||eyes}}, {{cog|hy|ակն}}, {{cog|ae|𐬀𐬱𐬌|t=eyes}}, {{cog|sa|अक्षि||tr=ákṣi}}. Related to [[ogle]].

The uncommon plural form {{m|en|eyen}} is from {{inh|en|enm|eyen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ēaġan}}, nominative and accusative plural of {{m|ang|ēaġe|t=eye}}.

